WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.050 --> 00:00:02.881
Here are the first two
places where the products,

2
00:00:02.881 --> 00:00:05.075
used as shipped, fall short of the loop.

3
00:00:05.075 --> 00:00:06.625
Gap one is the big one.

4
00:00:06.625 --> 00:00:10.035
SailPoint's own best practices
say the mapped ServiceNow

5
00:00:10.035 --> 00:00:13.588
status decides when a provisioning
task counts as complete.

6
00:00:13.588 --> 00:00:17.138
That's exactly what Book 13
calls closure by assertion.

7
00:00:17.138 --> 00:00:20.990
Our guidance: close the ServiceNow
record only on evidence,

8
00:00:20.990 --> 00:00:25.787
the next aggregation or a native-change
event showing the intended state.

9
00:00:25.787 --> 00:00:27.951
Gap two is about who approves.

10
00:00:27.951 --> 00:00:33.378
Book 15 says access an owner governs is
decided in the identity governance platform,

11
00:00:33.378 --> 00:00:36.712
but the catalog app moves
approval into ServiceNow.

12
00:00:36.712 --> 00:00:41.074
The fix is to choose one approver system
per authority class and write it down.

13
00:00:41.074 --> 00:00:42.530
Two more gaps to go.
